# coerce-floor golden — emitted-Go runtime-narrowing token census, BY COST CLASS.
#
# adapter  — the site produces a `reflect.MakeFunc` thunk (`rt.Coerce[func(…)…]`).
#            Cost is paid per INVOCATION of the adapted func — once per element of
#            every traversal it reaches. Statically closeable (doc 14 §5.1).
#            EXACT MATCH: any drift fails. `--bless` REFUSES to raise it.
# dispatch — `rt.SkyCall`, reflect call dispatch. doc 14 §4.3 irreducible floor.
#            FAIL-ON-INCREASE.
# narrow   — a value narrowing: at most one assertion (or one container rebuild)
#            per evaluation of the site. FAIL-ON-INCREASE.
#
# A DECREASE in dispatch/narrow is fine (floor tightened) — re-bless to ratchet down.
# Regenerate with: cargo run -p xtask -- coerce-floor --bless
# Re-key (adds/moves rows) with: cargo run -p xtask -- coerce-floor --rekey,
#   which additionally asserts sum(tokens) and count(rows) did not FALL.
# Format: <key>\tadapter=<n>\tdispatch=<n>\tnarrow=<n>
#   <key> without `/` is an examples/ directory; with `/` it is a
#   repo-root-relative Layer-2 project path (apps/manifest.toml).
#
# `dispatch` is 0 for every row: `rt.SkyCall` is reached from the runtime, not
# emitted into main.go by this compiler. The column is an armed tripwire for a
# lowering that starts emitting it, NOT a record of one that was eliminated.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-08-15 — eta-expansion of func-slot values ──
# `perf(lower): eta-expand a func value into a func slot, not rt.Coerce`
# replaced a func-shape `rt.Coerce` with a closure at the slot's shape whose
# parameters narrow inward. A 1-ary callback trades one coarse token for one
# precise one; an N-ary callback trades ONE for N — so `adapter` falls and
# `narrow` RISES on the projects whose callbacks are N-ary.
#
# That rise is the trade, not a regression. The token removed could never
# satisfy its own `v.(T)` fast path and allocated a []reflect.Value on every
# invocation; the tokens added are assertions that succeed. Measured on the
# Std.Ui marker scan: 318 -> 126 allocations per scan, 1.36x end-to-end
# throughput (docs/perf/runs/hof-dispatch-20260815/).
#
# Measured across the 56 projects that emit both before (b131e751) and after,
# by running THIS census against both compilers:
#     adapter  269 -> 24   (-245, -91%); 24 projects driven to 0; 0 rose
#     narrow  8055 -> 8234 (+179)
#     total   8324 -> 8258 (-66)
# The 24 residual adapters are `func_shape_eta`'s documented `None` returns —
# arity mismatch, non-symbol source, and a param/result whose narrowing would
# REBUILD a slice or map (trading an O(1) reflect box for an O(n) copy). They
# are locked here exactly, so closing any of them shows up as a gate failure
# asking to record the win.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-08-16 — the typed-lowering stages, blessed at
#    FULL corpus coverage ──
# This is the first bless taken with all 61 rows MEASURED in the same run.
# The four preceding stages were each verified against whatever subset the
# measuring machine could emit: on a clean checkout that is 56 of 61, because
# 03-tea-external, 05-mux-server, 08-notes-app and 11-fyne-stopwatch need a
# generated `sky-ffi/` surface and 13-skyshop an unfetched Sky dependency, and
# both `sky-ffi/` and `.skydeps/` are .gitignore'd. The gate filed those under
# "did not emit (not gated)" and reported PASS on the remainder, so a
# "no project rose" verdict covered 56 rows while reading as though it
# covered 61. That is now a hard failure with its own clause; see the module
# header of coerce_floor_gate.rs.
#
# Measured with all five surfaces restored, and cross-checked in two
# independent working trees that agreed to the token:
#     adapter  35 -> 28   (-7): 35-composite-generics 6 -> 2, apps/fieldbook 4 -> 1
#     narrow  9024 -> 8325 (-699) across 29 projects; NONE rose
#     total   9059 -> 8353 (-706)
# The `adapter` fall is the exact-match ratchet doing its job: both projects
# closed adapters the golden still reserved slack for, and that slack is now
# gone. The `narrow` fall is a decrease in SITE count and is not a speedup
# measurement — nothing here weights a site by how often it runs.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-21 — Model-subset field-type disambiguation ──
#     narrow  12858 -> 12850 (-8); 13-skyshop 1479 -> 1481 (+2), all other
#             moves are DECREASES; NO other project rose.
# A CORRECTNESS fix (lower/src/goty.rs `model_subset_resolves`). A row that is a
# NAME-subset of the TEA Model used to resolve to the nominal Model on field
# names alone. When a shared field is `Maybe X` in the Model but bare `X` in
# ANOTHER record nominal (`Model.clinic : Maybe Clinic` vs `ClinicRow.clinic :
# Clinic`), a `\r -> r.clinic.field` lambda over a `List ClinicRow` inferred the
# subset `{ clinic | ρ }` and mis-resolved it to the Model — rendering `r.clinic`
# as `SkyMaybe[Clinic]` and `r.clinic.field` as a static access on a `SkyMaybe`,
# which `go build` REJECTS (`sky check` passed: an "if it compiles it works"
# break, found in a real app). The fix vetoes the Model resolution for that
# wrap/unwrap ambiguity, so the row falls to the sound reflective (`any`) path.
# 13-skyshop carries one genuine instance of the same shape, hence +2; the net
# is a decrease. Guard: rust/crates/sky/tests/codegen_model_subset_record_lambda_flow.rs.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-24 — v0.25.17 app-surface sweep ──
#     narrow  12850 -> 13005 (+155) over 75 rows; adapter and dispatch
#             unchanged (0); no row fell. 31 rows +4, 3 rows +8, one +7 —
#             every rise is one of the three stdlib sources below.
# 1. +4 in every Std.App project: `Std.App.runTuiBoot_` gained a `withLine_`
#    step (terminal:tui now honours `App.withInput`, audit SA-10), in both its
#    `ViewUi` and `ViewString` branches. Each step carries the same two tokens
#    as the `withOnKey` step beside it: an R2 `rt.AsString` inside the eta
#    wrapper that retypes the `String -> msg` callback at the `Tui_withOnLine`
#    kernel slot (doc 14 §3 R2, already the closed form), and an R6/R8
#    generic-erase `rt.Coerce[any]` on the `Maybe (String -> msg)` payload of
#    the stdlib `App` record (doc 14 §4.5, blocked for stdlib ADTs).
# 2. +4 more in 37-composite-live-shop / 38-composite-ui-multibackend:
#    `Std.Ui.Input.wrapWithClickableLabel` (checkbox / radio labels are real
#    `<label>` elements, audit UF-13) reads the stdlib `Label` payload: four
#    R6 narrowings, the same shape as the existing `wrapWithLabel`.
#    apps/fieldbook is the third +8 row (sources 1 and 2).
# 3. 67-durable-counter +7 = source 1 (+4), plus `Std.Durable.loadSnapshot` +1
#    (a snapshot that no longer decodes is now a classified Decode error, not
#    `Nothing`, audit SA-8) and `Sky.Core.Error.toString` +2 (now reachable, to
#    log that error).
# Found by bisecting the SOURCE (a compiler at d08a5910 and at main 0d34d2e7
# both measure 20-cli-counter at 49; the sweep measures 53, all in
# runTuiBoot_).
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-24 — v0.25.17 UI/UX sweep fixes ──
#     narrow +5 -1 over 6 rows; adapter and dispatch unchanged (0). Every rise
#     sits in a function whose SOURCE changed (per-function token diff):
# 1. +1 in 37 / 38 / apps/fieldbook: the checkbox overlay (later REVERTED —
#    see the next record; 38 falls back). In 37 and apps/fieldbook the +1 that
#    remains is `Std.Ui.Input.radioRow` / `radio` gaining the
#    `data-sky-radio-group` marker attr (radio groups name their radios),
#    measured per function against main: radioRow 2 -> 3.
# 2. +1 26-ui-showcase: `Edit s` now binds its String payload (the textarea
#    edits a model field), one R6 payload narrowing in `Main_update`.
# 3. +1 62-app-notes: `Persist.createNote` answers the inserted id (an `Int`
#    out of `Task.run`), one R2 scalar narrowing.
# 4. -1 63-app-chat: the record-alias field fix (`LoadResp.messages` is
#    `[]Domain_Message_R`, no longer converted through the stdlib
#    `Std_Ai_Provider_Message_R`) removes one narrowing. Floor tightened.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-24 (later) — ratchet DOWN after the sweep ──
#     narrow  13-skyshop 1485 -> 1468 (-17): its sixteen `!=` were an unknown
#             operator the resolver lowered to `rt.Add` (each an `rt.AsBool`
#             narrowing); they are `/=` now and `!=` is `[E1014]`.
#             38-composite-ui-multibackend 326 -> 325 (-1): its checkbox icon
#             is a check mark beside the native box instead of a drawn box.
#     No row rose. Blessed so the lower floor is locked.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-25 — v0.25.18 parser-safe Std.Ui nesting ──
#     narrow +4 in each of 7 rows (+28, 12991 -> 13019); adapter and dispatch
#     unchanged (0). Rows: 52-blog-analytics, 61-app-kanban, 62-app-notes,
#     63-app-chat, 64-app-native, apps/fieldbook, examples/60-spa-todos/client.
#     Cause (2), a STDLIB source change: Std.Ui renders every element under a
#     `Nesting` state so it never emits a nesting the HTML parser restructures
#     (a block inside <p>, a link inside a link, …), which made Sky.Spa SSR
#     hydration refuse and rebuild the page. Per-function token diff of
#     63-app-chat's emitted Go against v0.25.17: every delta sits in a function
#     whose source changed — renderElement -> renderElementIn, renderNodeAs,
#     layoutWith, and the new keptRoleAttrs. No function whose source is
#     unchanged moved.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-25 — v0.25.19 FFI function values ──
#     narrow  13-skyshop 1468 -> 1479 (+11); adapter and dispatch unchanged (0);
#     no other row moved. Cause: a CODEGEN FIX that adds code where there was
#     none. Eleven Go-FFI functions passed as VALUES in src/Lib/Stripe.sky
#     (`Result.andThen Stripe.addressLine1`, `...CustomerDetailsName`, …) used
#     to lower to `nil` — no code, so no narrowing, and a NilDereference panic
#     when applied. Each now lowers to a closure over its wrapper that pays
#     exactly what a CALL of that wrapper pays: one `rt.Coerce` of the argument
#     into the wrapper's `FfiT_…_P0` slot (the Go-FFI argument floor, doc 14
#     §4). Measured on the emitted Go: 11 closures, one tracked token each.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-27 — v0.27 session-id rotation ──
#     narrow  67-durable-counter 89 -> 90 (+1); adapter and dispatch unchanged
#     (0); no other row moved. Cause (2), a STDLIB source change: the
#     `App.DurableWiring` record gained a `discard : String -> Task Error ()`
#     field (`Durable.deleteSnapshot`), which Sky.Live calls when a session id
#     is retired (rotation at sign-in, revocation, Live.endSession) so a
#     retired id restores nothing. The one new token is the field's copy into
#     the Live wiring record, the same narrowing the sibling `persist` field
#     already pays there. Only the one durable example builds that record.
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-28 — v0.27 Go-FFI calls typed from their
#    pinned signature ──
#     narrow  03-tea-external 4 -> 5 (+1), 05-mux-server 10 -> 11 (+1),
#             13-skyshop 1479 -> 1509 (+30); adapter and dispatch unchanged
#             (0); no other row moved (the other FFI rows, 02/07/08/11, are
#             unchanged). Nothing got less typed: the reverse. A Go-FFI call
#             used to type as a free variable, so its `Result`'s ERROR
#             parameter stayed `any` wherever usage did not pin it. It now
#             types from the binding's `skyType`, whose error is
#             `Sky.Core.Error.Error`, so the subject is
#             `rt.SkyResult[Sky_Core_Error_Error, A]` like every kernel Result.
#             The existing case-pattern lowering reads a ctor field as `any` and
#             narrows it to the binder's type, so each `Err e ->` branch over an
#             FFI result now binds `e` through one
#             `rt.Coerce[Sky_Core_Error_Error](_subj.ErrValue)` — measured on
#             the emitted Go (sky check, before/after): 0 -> 1 (03), 0 -> 1
#             (05), 33 -> 61 (13-skyshop). The assertion runs only on the error
#             path. The remaining skyshop delta is String params of unannotated
#             helpers now inferred from the FFI signatures they call: the
#             `rt.AsString` moves from inside the helper to its call sites.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-09-28 — v0.27 phase 7: typed payload patterns ──
#   narrow 13063 -> 12171 (-892), 52 rows tightened, none raised, adapter 0.
#   `bind_field_pat` (lower.rs) now reads `.OkValue` / `.ErrValue` /
#   `.JustValue` of a subject whose Go type already types the field at that
#   type, instead of `rt.Coerce[T]` / `rt.AsInt` / `rt.AsString` around it
#   (doc 14 R8, lever 5.2). Evidence: the emitted Go of all 75 projects was
#   dumped with the change and with it reverted; the reverted build reproduced
#   the old golden (13063) exactly, and every one of the 892 removed tokens sits
#   in a diff hunk that reads a container payload field, with no hunk adding a
#   token. This also returns the +32 the FFI-typing transition above recorded.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-02 — v0.27.1: open rows no longer captured
#    by an alias with the same field set ──
#   narrow +8 over 3 rows (16-skychess 563 -> 565, 66-slack-agent 140 -> 142,
#   apps/ledger 502 -> 506), adapter 0, no other row moved (71 of 75 measured;
#   the 4 FFI rows are UNMEASURED under SKY_LIVE_TESTS=skip, as in CI).
#   A soundness fix that WIDENS (doc 14 §9.8, origin R10/R11, policy floor):
#   an open row resolved by field set to an alias a wider record could not
#   survive (a `Request` crossing the Go boundary as a user `{ body }` alias
#   lost its cookies). Each delta was checked in the emitted Go against v0.27.0:
#   skychess and slack-agent read a user/stdlib record through `rt.Field`
#   instead of `rt.Coerce` to an unrelated stdlib alias (`Std.Durable.ResultRow`,
#   `Std.Ai.Provider.RawChoice`); ledger's `addAccount` form parameter is now
#   `any` because another nominal collects the same three fields and more.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-12 — v0.28.0 Std.Ai lifecycle, traced ──
#   Measured against origin/main 03d61922f (76 of 80 rows; 03-tea-external,
#   05-mux-server, 08-notes-app and 13-skyshop are UNMEASURED under
#   SKY_LIVE_TESTS=skip). adapter 0, dispatch 0. Rows at or below origin/main:
#   09-live-counter 125 (= origin): the wider-nominal check on an open row
#     (goty.rs `wider_nominal_could_carry`, doc 14 §9.8, R10/R11) now counts
#     only record aliases of modules the program loads (lower.rs
#     `program_type_closure`). `Std.Ai.Eval.ScorerScore { scorer, mean, count }`
#     no longer widens the unannotated `viewCounter` row `{ count | r }`.
#   apps/relay 175 (origin 176): `Error.isRetryable` / `domain` / `retryAfter`
#     are typed runtime kernels (rt/error_kernels.go) reached through
#     `kernel_typed_return_twin` (lower.rs, R5, lever §5.3): no Sky payload
#     read of the erased `Sky_Core_Error` ADT, no narrowed kernel return.
#   Rows new since origin/main (measured here, no origin value):
#   68-ai-dataset 548, 69-ai-scrub 99, 70-ai-synthetic 696, 71-ai-registry 956,
#   sky-bundled/ai 656. They fell from 626 / 99 / 769 / 1057 / 734, mostly
#   because `Std.Ai.Failure` reads each constructor payload once (`facts`, one
#   match for the message and the attributes, R6) and decodes through
#   monomorphic helpers instead of `Maybe.map` lambdas (R12 via R1); the Error
#   kernels and the Provider rewrite below account for the rest.
#   The two rows this note listed as still above origin/main
#   (66-slack-agent 147, sky-bundled/console 330) were closed by the next
#   transition.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-12 — typed kernel returns (R5, §5.3) ──
#   narrow 14423 -> 12669 (-1754), 61 rows tightened, none raised, adapter 0,
#   dispatch 0, all 80 rows measured (the four FFI examples after `sky install`).
#   `kernel_typed_return_twin` (lower.rs) routes a fully applied
#   String.fromInt / toUpper / toLower / startsWith / endsWith / contains /
#   join / left / right / dropLeft / dropRight, Encoding.urlEncode, Basics.not
#   and Json.Encode.encode call to a runtime twin that returns the result's Go
#   type, so the call site narrows nothing. A twin parameter typed `int` /
#   `string` / `bool` / `[]string` is used only when the argument lowers to
#   exactly that type (doc 14 §1, per call site); otherwise the erased call
#   stays. An empty list literal in a typed slot is built at the slot's type
#   (R1, §5.2). Twins are checked against the erased kernels in
#   runtime-go/rt/kernel_twins_test.go; the rt package builds for wasm.
#   Every row is now at or below origin/main 03d61922f: 66-slack-agent 136
#   (origin 142), sky-bundled/console 204 (origin 292), apps/relay 142
#   (origin 176), 09-live-counter 101 (origin 125). The four rows that were
#   UNMEASURED without a generated FFI surface now measure 03-tea-external 3,
#   05-mux-server 3, 08-notes-app 361 (was carried at 403), 13-skyshop 1194
#   (was carried at 1260).
